            descriptionCourte = "Raspberry-red patches in a grey matrix, nicknamed the \"drunkard's stone\".",
            descriptionLongue = "Eudialyte forms raspberry-red to pink patches and veins in a grey alkaline rock (often associated with nepheline), earning it the nickname \"drunkard's stone\" in Russia. Rarely faceted in pure form, it is mainly used as cabochons or tumbled stones.",
            particularites = "Almost always sold as a cabochon or rough-polished stone, rarely faceted due to its partial opacity.",
            lithotherapie = "Nicknamed the stone of self-love, eudialyte is used to soothe emotional wounds and foster self-acceptance."
